","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Epidemiology","volume":"40"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105007672762"],"search":{"DAF":["ALK-Abello A/S","Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Private Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","danbio"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ed9ac142-b1da-4775-9fa9-c44d1679fa45","au-188bade2-a9a2-4d12-883d-5d064d52ff97","ku-8bde7dc9-711a-4d82-96b4-b5ea91d26a9a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cohort profile: Copenhagen Hospital Biobank‑chronic inflammatory disease—inflammatory bowel disease (CHB‑CID:IBD) genetic cohort","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-094.41-813496","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Parkinson’s disease involves the accumulation of aggregates of ɑ-synuclein (ɑ-Syn), both as intracellular fibrils and as cytotoxic soluble oligomeric species (ɑSOs). No available nanobodies show exclusive preference for the oligomeric state of ɑ-Syn. Here, we describe two nanobodies NB1 and NB2, obtained by immunizing a llama with αSOs, which bind ɑSOs with nM affinity and do not show any measurable affinity for monomeric ɑ-Syn or ɑ-Syn fibrils. While the nanobodies were not useful for high-throughput screening for therapeutic compounds or high-resolution cryoEM, they retained their ability to discriminate against ɑ-Syn monomers in brain tissue and were able to detect ɑ-Syn aggregates in diseased tissue. In addition, αSO binding affinity was improved by DNA-scaffold-mediated NB1 dimerization compared to scaffolded monomeric NB1. The nanobodies promote the uptake of ɑSOs into HEK93 cells via the Sortilin receptor pathway. Their absolute specificity for oligomeric ɑ-Syn makes them promising reagents to detect oligomeric ɑ-Syn in patient samples.","author_count":35,"contributors":["Nielsen, Janni","Pedersen, Jannik N.","Kleijwegt, Giulia","Nowak, Jan S.","Nami, Faranak","Johansen, Charlie","Sassetti, Elisa","Berg, Bjørn Bjerre","Lyngsø, Nanna Miang","Brøchner, Bo Volf","Carlson, Johanne Holm","Simonsen, Amanda","Olsen, William Pallisgaard","Simonsen, Bine Wissendorf","Mikkelsen, Jakob Hauge","Sereika-Bejder, Vita","Aarup Lauritsen, Johanne","Merrild, Kirstine Friis","Malle, Mette Galsgaard","Valero, Julián","Kjems, Jørgen","Bøggild, Andreas","Boesen, Thomas","Birkelund, Svend","Christiansen, Gunna","Hansen, Simon Boje","Kristensen, Marianne","Madsen, Peder Søndergaard","Strømgaard, Kristian","Romero-Ramos, Marina","Gustafsen, Camilla","Glerup, Simon","Andersen, Kasper Røjkjær","Clausen, Mads Hartvig","Otzen, Daniel E."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-823961"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Otzen, Daniel E."],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nanobodies raised against the cytotoxic α synuclein oligomer are oligomer specific and promote its cellular uptake","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s44328-025-00042-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-823961","ids":["aau-c67acccb-33d2-4cc3-aeda-6b98b8c1a78a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-920093B5A59F7B97A017C0AF9D59C49B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s44328-025-00042-1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/789778735/s44328-025-00042-1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-P