"orcid":"0000-0002-0144-1305","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Roni","key":"nielsenbentroniranghøjpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"896f4a21-d29c-4ad9-b0ef-4e7f8616c234","name":"Nielsen, Bent Roni Ranghøj","name_org":"Nielsen, Roni","orcid":"0000-0001-9228-3869","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"wiggershenrikpau","last":"Wiggers","locid":"aef6a13e-8c07-474c-a4f6-bc35236a6eda","name":"Wiggers, Henrik","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38563382"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/jaha.123.033628","issn":["20479980"],"issue":"8","journal":"Journal of the American Heart Association","paperid":"e033628","publisher":"American Heart Association Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of the American Heart Association","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85190900736"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b5468f33-d70d-4e6b-aa2c-2253001e1203"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Enantiomer-Specific Cardiovascular Effects of the Ketone Body 3-Hydroxybutyrate","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-737579","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND AIMS: Despite advances in the medical treatment of Crohn's disease (CD), many patients will still need bowel resections and face the subsequent risk of recurrence and re-resection. We describe contemporary re-resection rates and identify disease-modifying factors and risk factors for re-resection. METHODS: We conducted a retrospective, population-based, individual patient data cohort study covering 47.4% of the Danish population, including all CD patients who underwent a primary resection between 2010 and 2020. RESULTS: Among 631 primary resected patients, 24.5% underwent a second resection, and 5.3% a third. Re-resection rates after one, five, and 10 years were 12.6%, 22.4%, and 32.2%, respectively. Reasons for additional resections were mainly disease activity (57%) and stoma reversal (40%). Disease activity-driven re-resection rates after one, five, and 10 years were 3.6%, 10.1%, and 14.1%, respectively. Most stoma reversals occurred within one year (80%). The median time to recurrence was 11.0 months. Biologics started within one year of the first resection revealed protective effect against re-resection for stenotic and penetrating phenotypes. Prophylactic biologic therapy at primary ileocecal resection reduced disease recurrence and re-resection risk (HR 0.58, 95% CI (0.34-0.99), p=0.047). Risk factors for re-resection were location of resected bowel segments at the primary resection, disease location, disease behavior, smoking, and perianal disease. CONCLUSION: Re-resection rates, categorized by disease activity, are lower than those reported in other studies and are closely associated with disease phenotype and localization. Biological therapy may be disease-modifying for certain subgroups when initiated within one year of resection.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Poulsen, Anja","Rasmussen, Julie","Wewer, Mads Damsgaard","Hansen, Esben Holm","Nordestgaard, Rie Louise Møller","Jespersen, Hans Søe Riis","Christiansen, Dagmar","Surnacheva, Elena","Lin, Viviane Annabelle","Aydemir, Nurcan","Verlo, Kari Anne","Pachler, Frederik Rønne","Ovesen, Pernille Dige","Fuglsang, Kristian Asp","Brandt, Christopher Filtenborg","Sørensen, Lars Tue","Krarup, Peter-Martin","Gögenur, Ismail","Burisch, Johan","Seidelin, Jakob Benedict"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-777045"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"re resection rates and disease recurrence in crohn s disease a population based study using individual level patient data","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-777045","identifier":[{"id":"85206597804","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38727089","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-168b400f-f5ea-4a8e-aae9-0231c0c6bcc7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3CEAF5AE281128F1AA3DF0EEAAA57981"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg","Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Køge"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U",