{"abstract":"Trace element polluted soils pose risks to human and environmental health. Biochar can decrease trace element bioavailability in soils, but their resulting ability to reduce soil toxicity may vary significantly depending on feedstocks used, pyrolysis conditions, and the target pollutants. Chromated copper arsenate (CCA) polluted sites are common, but only very few types of biochar have been tested for these sites. Hence, we tested fourteen well-characterized biochar materials for their ability to bind Cu and reduce toxicity in a CCA polluted soil in a 56-day experiment. Biochar (1%, wt/wt) increased plant (wheat, Triticum aestivum L.) shoot and root growth by 6–58% and 0–73%, reduced soil toxicity to Arthrobacter globiformis by 7–55%, decreased bioavailable Cu (Pseudomonas fluorescens bioreporter) by 5–65%, and decreased free Cu2+ ion activities by 27–89%. The A. globiformis solid-contact test constituted a sensitive ecotoxicological endpoint and deserves further attention for assessment of soil quality. Oil seed rape straw biochar generally performed better than other tested biochar materials. Biochar performance was positively correlated with its high cation exchange capacity, multiple surface functional groups, and high nitrogen and phosphorus content. Our results pave the way for future selection of feedstocks for creation of modified biochar materials with optimal performance in CCA polluted soil.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Tang, Yinqi","Wang, Chen","Holm, Peter Engelund","Hansen, Hans Chr. Bruun","Brandt, Kristian Koefoed"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-690293"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impacts of biochar materials on copper speciation bioavailability and toxicity in chromated copper arsenate polluted soil","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jhazmat.2023.132067","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-690293","identifier":[{"id":"37478594","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85166759484","type":"scopus"},{"id":"001046975600001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-bbb4c361-84cd-4f94-8b3e-4a8120eec821"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5E8AF1D5D87A61EF8C1221AC9B20D533"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/363060807/Impacts_of_biochar_materials_on_copper_speciation_bioavailability_and_toxicity_in_chromated_copper_arsenate_polluted_soil.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jhazmat.2023.132067","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Microbial Ecology and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Yinqi","key":"tangpau","last":"Tang","locid":"218ef61a-aeb2-4e93-b324-b6dc24151f75","name":"Tang, Yinqi","orcid":"0000-0002-6407-6990","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Chen","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"841efacf-bff8-48ef-8142-b6bd2525250b","name":"Wang, Chen","orcid":"0000-0002-3271-5516","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter Engelund","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"cc41fec2-bb93-4070-abe0-b4f120b183a8","name":"Holm, Peter Engelund","orcid":"0000-0003-1233-0843","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans Chr. Bruun","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"9b553aa7-aebe-452e-b36f-b21edcff4e70","name":"Hansen, Hans Chr. Bruun","orcid":"0000-0002-8617-2393","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristian Koefoed","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"c196f0ea-2378-4bc3-bf49-2e64410cbabf","name":"Brandt, Kristian Koefoed","orcid":"0000-0001-7886-9708","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37478594"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jhazmat.2023.132067","issn":["03043894","18733336"],"issn_org":["03043894"],"journal":"Journal of Hazardous Materials","paperid":"132067","status":"p","title":"Journal of Hazardous Materials","volume":"459"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85166759484"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-bbb4c361-84cd-4f94-8b3e-4a8120eec821"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Impacts of biochar materials on copper speciation, bioavailability, and toxicity in chromated copper arsenate polluted soil","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-690293","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Metformin and exercise both improve glycemic control, but in vitro studies have indicated that an interaction between metformin and exercise occurs in skeletal muscle, suggesting a blunting effect of metformin on exercise training adaptations. Two studies (a double-blind, parallel-group, randomized clinical trial conducted in 29 glucose-intolerant individuals and a double-blind, cross-over trial conducted in 15 healthy lean males) were included in this paper. In both studies, the effect of acute exercise ± metformin treatment on different skeletal muscle variables, previously suggested to be involved in a pharmaco-physiological interaction between metformin and exercise, was assessed. Furthermore, in the parallel-group trial, the effect of 12 weeks of exercise training was assessed. Skeletal muscle biopsies were obtained before and after acute exercise and 12 weeks of exercise training, and mitochondrial respiration, oxidative stress and AMPK activation was determined. Metformin did not significantly affect the effects of acute exercise or exercise training on mitochondrial respiration, oxidative stress or AMPK activation, indicating that the response to acute exercise and exercise training adaptations in skeletal muscle is not affected by metformin treatment. Further studies are needed to investigate whether an interaction between metformin and exercise is present in other tissues, e.g. the gut.  Trial registration: ClinicalTrials.gov (NCT03316690 and NCT02951260). ","author_count":19,"contributors":["Pilmark, Nanna Skytt","Oberholzer, Laura","Halling, Jens Frey","Kristensen, Jonas Møller","Bønding, Christina Pedersen","Elkjær, Ida","Lyngbæk, Mark","Elster, Grit","Siebenmann, Christoph","Holm, Niels Frederich","Birk, Jesper Bratz","Larsen, Emil List","Meinild-Lundby, Anne-Kristine","Wojtaszewski, Jørgen","Pilegaard, Henriette","Poulsen, Henrik","Pedersen, Bente Klarlund","Hansen, Katrine Bagge","Karstoft, Kristian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-492756"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","EURAC Research"],"keyword":["AMPK","Exercise","Faculty of Science","Impaired glucose tolerance","Interaction","Metformin","Prediabetes","ROS","Skeletal muscle","Training"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Institute of Mountain Emergency Medicine"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"skeletal muscle adaptations to exercise are not influenced by metformin treatment in humans secondary analyses of 000000000002 randomised clinical trials","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/284840726/Pilmark_et_al_Applied_Physiology_Nutrition_and_Metabolism_2021_0194_Accepted_manuscript_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-492756","identifier":[{"id":"85125882448","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34784247","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-a64ae10a-385d-41e8-8d10-227fc24a5914"],"keyword":["AMPK","Complex-1","Exercise","Faculty of Science","Healthy lean males","Impaired glucose tolerance","Interaction","Metformin","Prediabetes","ROS","Skeletal muscle","Training"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1D462A35EA0FC00A15B0BB358400D505"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/284840726/Pilmark_et_al_Applied_Physiology_Nutrition_and_Metabolism_2021_0194_Accepted_manuscript_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Institute of Mountain Emergency Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"it","key":"eurac research","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"EURAC Research","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Nanna Skytt","key":"pilmarkpau","last":"Pilmark","locid":"0e9899b9-7875-4cd3-9d02-3cfe1ddaccf5","name":"Pilmark, Nanna Skytt","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Laura","key":"oberholzerpau","last":"Oberholzer","locid":"ef9c4eab-6f8d-45e0-9642-3bdc48aaca9f","name":"Oberholzer, Laura","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Frey","key":"hallingpau","last":"Halling","locid":"8ff050ee-4eac-4e48-be9a-625f63d227b6","name":"Halling, Jens Frey","orcid":"0000-0002-8638-6746","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas Møller","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"d4a04b8e-a355-4db2-8e28-1592c24a3f2e","name":"Kristensen, Jonas Møller","orcid":"0000-0002-8296-975X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christina Pedersen","key":"bøndingpau","last":"Bønding","name":"Bønding, Christina Pedersen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ida","key":"elkjærpau","last":"Elkjær","name":"Elkjær, Ida","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Mark","key":"lyngbækpau","last":"Lyngbæk","locid":"89277a1c-1e09-473b-adc0-dc4b531f9198","name":"Lyngbæk, Mark","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Grit","key":"elsterpau","last":"Elster","name":"Elster, Grit","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 4","first":"Christoph","key":"siebenmannpau","last":"Siebenmann","name":"Siebenmann, Christoph","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Niels Frederich","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, Niels Frederich","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Bratz","key":"birkpau","last":"Birk","locid":"03b94e42-79b2-4498-9c5b-cfb4e38e17c8","name":"Birk, Jesper Bratz","orcid":"0000-0001-9775-4789","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Emil List","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Emil List","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anne-Kristine","key":"meinildlundbypau","last":"Meinild-Lundby","name":"Meinild-Lundby, Anne-Kristine","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jørgen","key":"wojtaszewskipau","last":"Wojtaszewski","locid":"06441180-44ed-4f23-b077-4d90876cc68b","name":"Wojtaszewski, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0001-8185-3408","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henriette","key":"pilegaardpau","last":"Pilegaard","locid":"bca00b25-e11a-407d-936f-6982a39ef1d8","name":"Pilegaard, Henriette","orcid":"0000-0002-1071-0327","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Henrik","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"8ae87c93-48de-4c57-82c4-7769e337fe89","name":"Poulsen, Henrik","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Bente Klarlund","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"5d38d54e-e0d1-4397-98ca-6d8c9b78606d","name":"Pedersen, Bente Klarlund","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Katrine Bagge","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Katrine Bagge","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Kristian","key":"karstoftpau","last":"Karstoft","locid":"80f306e9-a560-493c-b7d4-4e18b694660f","name":"Karstoft, Kristian","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34784247"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1139/apnm-2021-0194","issn":["17155312","17155320"],"issn_org":["17155312"],"issue":"3","journal":"Applied Physiology, Nutrition and Metabolism","pages":"309-320","status":"p","title":"Applied Physiology, Nutrition and Metabolism","volume":"47"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85125882448"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a64ae10a-385d-41e8-8d10-227fc24a5914"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Skeletal muscle adaptations to exercise are not influenced by metformin treatment in humans: secondary analyses of 2 randomised, clinical trials","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-492756","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The established causal genes in Alzheimer's disease (AD), APP, PSEN1, and PSEN2, are functionally characterized using biomarkers, capturing an in vivo profile reflecting the disease's initial preclinical phase. Mutations in SORL1, encoding the endosome recycling receptor SORLA, are found in 2%-3% of individuals with early-onset AD, and SORL1 haploinsufficiency appears to be causal for AD. To test whether SORL1 can function as an AD causal gene, we use CRISPR-Cas9-based gene editing to develop a model of SORL1 haploinsufficiency in Göttingen minipigs, taking advantage of porcine models for biomarker investigations. SORL1 haploinsufficiency in young adult minipigs is found to phenocopy the preclinical in vivo profile of AD observed with APP, PSEN1, and PSEN2, resulting in elevated levels of β-amyloid (Aβ) and tau preceding amyloid plaque formation and neurodegeneration, as observed in humans. Our study provides functional support for the theory that SORL1 haploinsufficiency leads to endosome cytopathology with biofluid hallmarks of autosomal dominant AD.","author_count":27,"contributors":["Andersen, Olav M.","Bøgh, Nikolaj","Landau, Anne M.","Pløen, Gro G.","Jensen, Anne Mette G.","Monti, Giulia","Ulhøi, Benedicte P.","Nyengaard, Jens R.","Jacobsen, Kirsten R.","Jørgensen, Margarita M.","Holm, Ida Elisabeth Gad","Kristensen, Marianne L.","Alstrup, Aage Kristian O.","Hansen, Esben S. S.","Teunissen, Charlotte E.","Breidenbach, Laura","Droescher, Mathias","Liu, Ying","Pedersen, Hanne S.","Callesen, Henrik","Luo, Yonglun","Bolund, Lars","Brooks, David J.","Laustsen, Christoffer","Small, Scott A.","Mikkelsen, Lars F.","Sørensen, Charlotte B."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-006535"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Olav M.","Andersen, Olav Michael","Sørensen, Charlot