-1c874198a115"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A genetically modified minipig model for Alzheimer's disease with SORL1 haploinsufficiency","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-006535","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: Self-reported psychological stress has been associated with decreased semen quality. Cortisol levels in scalp hair (hair cortisol concentration, HCC) has emerged as a potential objective marker of psychological stress. Thus, we investigated if HCC was associated with markers of testicular function. Furthermore, we examined whether three common single nucleotide polymorphisms in the glucocorticoid-receptor gene (NR3C1, chromosome 5), potentially affecting receptor sensitivity, were associated with HCC and could influence the studied association between HCC and testicular function. DESIGN: Cross-sectional study. METHODS: We analysed HCC, serum-levels of reproductive hormones, semen parameters, and the three NR3C1-polymorphisms; BclI (rs41423247), Tth111I (rs10052957), and 9β (rs6198), in a population of 696 men from the general population. RESULTS: HCC was not associated with testicular function, and adjustment for the three NR3C1-polymorphisms did not alter the results. However, HCC increased significantly with the number of Tth111I minor-alleles (T) and decreased significantly with the number of 9β minor-alleles (G). CONCLUSION: Given previously shown associations between stress and semen quality, and that no association between HCC and self-reported stress was observed in the current study, we speculate that negative reproductive effects of stress may not be mediated directly by cortisol. This study demonstrates associations between HCC and glucocorticoid receptor gene variants indicating that these SNPs may influence systemic glucocorticoid levels, but the potential health effects of such alterations are yet unknown.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Nordkap, Loa","Almstrup, Kristian","Priskorn, Lærke","Bang, Anne Kirstine","Stalder, Tobias","Petersen, Jørgen Holm","Hansen, Åse Marie","Juul, Anders","Johannsen, Trine Holm","Jørgensen, Niels"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-768778"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Department of Clinical Psychology, University of Siegen, Siegen, Germany.","University of Siegen"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["The International Research and Research Training Centre in Endocrine Disruption of Male Reproduction and Child Health (EDMaRC), Rigshospitalet, University of Copenhagen, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hair cortisol glucocorticoid gene receptor polymorphisms stress and testicular function","src":["ku","nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85139218061","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-768778","identifier":[{"id":"36179533","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85139218061","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3ecb25b6-b0ea-47cd-966b-9e07c034552d","nfa-11aa415c-0f6f-4076-a00f-7762fe50d24b"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-876D89D8480C888E07D70B9D3259661A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["The International Research and Research Training Centre in Endocrine Disruption of Male Reproduction and Child Health (EDMaRC), Rigshospitalet, University of Copenhagen, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Molecular Aging Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"university of siegen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Siegen","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"department of clinical psychology university of siegen siegen germany","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Department of Clinical Psychology, University of Siegen, Siegen, Germany.","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"dk","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["National Research Center for the Working Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Loa","key":"nordkappau","last":"Nordkap","name":"Nordkap, Loa","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Kristian","key":"almstruppau","last":"Almstrup","locid":"6dcb9136-f13d-4486-916a-3e29ffb45147","name":"Almstrup, Kristian","orcid":"0000-0002-1832-0307","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Lærke","key":"priskornpau","last":"Priskorn","name":"Priskorn, Lærke","rank":3,