{"abstract":"Angiopoietin-like 4 (ANGPTL4) is an endogenous inhibitor of lipoprotein lipase that modulates lipid levels, coronary atherosclerosis risk, and nutrient partitioning. We hypothesize that loss of ANGPTL4 function might improve glucose homeostasis and decrease risk of type 2 diabetes (T2D). We investigate protein-altering variants in ANGPTL4 among 58,124 participants in the DiscovEHR human genetics study, with follow-up studies in 82,766 T2D cases and 498,761 controls. Carriers of p.E40K, a variant that abolishes ANGPTL4 ability to inhibit lipoprotein lipase, have lower odds of T2D (odds ratio 0.89, 95% confidence interval 0.85-0.92, p = 6.3 × 10 -10 ), lower fasting glucose, and greater insulin sensitivity. Predicted loss-of-function variants are associated with lower odds of T2D among 32,015 cases and 84,006 controls (odds ratio 0.71, 95% confidence interval 0.49-0.99, p = 0.041). Functional studies in Angptl4-deficient mice confirm improved insulin sensitivity and glucose homeostasis. In conclusion, genetic inactivation of ANGPTL4 is associated with improved glucose homeostasis and reduced risk of T2D.","author_count":81,"contributors":["Gusarova, Viktoria","O'Dushlaine, Colm","Teslovich, Tanya M.","Benotti, Peter N.","Mirshahi, Tooraj","Gottesman, Omri","Van Hout, Cristopher V.","Murray, Michael F.","Mahajan, Anubha","Nielsen, Jonas B.","Fritsche, Lars","Wulff, Anders Berg","Gudbjartsson, Daniel F.","Sjögren, Marketa","Emdin, Connor A.","Scott, Robert A.","Lee, Wen Jane","Small, Aeron","Kwee, Lydia C.","Dwivedi, Om Prakash","Prasad, Rashmi B.","Bruse, Shannon","Lopez, Alexander E.","Penn, John","Marcketta, Anthony","Leader, Joseph B.","Still, Christopher D.","Kirchner, H. Lester","Mirshahi, Uyenlinh L.","Wardeh, Amr H.","Hartle, Cassandra M.","Habegger, Lukas","Fetterolf, Samantha N.","Tusie-Luna, Teresa","Morris, Andrew P.","Holm, Hilma","Steinthorsdottir, Valgerdur","Sulem, Patrick","Thorsteinsdottir, Unnur","Rotter, Jerome I.","Chuang, Lee Ming","Damrauer, Scott","Birtwell, David","Brummett, Chad M.","Khera, Amit V.","Natarajan, Pradeep","Orho-Melander, Marju","Flannick, Jason","Lotta, Luca A.","Willer, Cristen J.","Holmen, Oddgeir L.","Ritchie, Marylyn D.","Ledbetter, David H.","Murphy, Andrew J.","Borecki, Ingrid B.","Reid, Jeffrey G.","Overton, John D.","Hansson, Ola","Groop, Leif","Shah, Svati H.","Kraus, William E.","Rader, Daniel J.","Chen, Yii Der I.","Hveem, Kristian","Wareham, Nicholas J.","Kathiresan, Sekar","Melander, Olle","Stefansson, Kari","Nordestgaard, Børge G","Tybjærg-Hansen, Anne","Abecasis, Goncalo R.","Altshuler, David","Florez, Jose C.","Boehnke, Michael","McCarthy, Mark I.","Yancopoulos, George D.","Carey, David J.","Shuldiner, Alan R.","Baras, Aris","Dewey, Frederick E.","Gromada, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-519128"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, Central","America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Estonia","Finland","Iceland","Mexico","Norway","Sweden","Taiwan","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Duke University","Geisinger","Harvard University","Helsingin Yliopisto","Instituto Nacional de Ciencias Medicas y Nutricion Salvador Zubiran","Lund University","Massachusetts Institute of Technology","National Taiwan University","Nord-Trøndelag Health Trust","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","Oxford University Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust","Regeneron Pharmaceuticals, Inc.","Tunghai University","Universidad Nacional Autónoma de México","University of California at Los Angeles","University of Cambridge","University of Liverpool","University of Michigan, Ann Arbor","University of Oxford","University of Pennsylvania","University of Tartu","VA Medical Center","Veterans General Hospital-Taichung Taiwan","deCODE Genetics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic inactivation of angptl000000000004 improves glucose homeostasis and is associated with reduced risk of diabetes","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-04611-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-519128","identifier":[{"id":"29899519","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5997992","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85048556517","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d25ff1f7-455a-4c11-87ed-edec55141ef1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-07DAD6407738A6C2182C1212B758BDBD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/217551589/s41467_018_04611_z.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-04611-z","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"regeneron pharmaceuticals inc","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Regeneron Pharmaceuticals, Inc.","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"geisinger","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Geisinger","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of michigan ann arbor","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Michigan, Ann Arbor","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":