{"abstract":"Bracken ferns (Pteridium spp.) are well-known for their carcinogenic properties, which are ascribed to the content of ptaquiloside and ptaquiloside-like substances. Ptaquiloside leach from the ferns and may cause contamination of drinking water. Pterosin B is formed by hydrolysis of ptaquiloside. In soil, Pterosin B is adsorbed more strongly and it is expected to have a slower turnover than ptaquiloside. We thus hypothesized that pterosin B may serve as an indicator for any past presence of ptaquiloside. Pterosin B degradation was studied in acid forest soils from bracken-covered and bracken-free areas. Soil samples were incubated with pterosin B at 3 and 8 μg g(-1) for 10 days, whereas sterile (autoclaved) samples were incubated for 23 days. Pterosin B showed unexpected fast degradation in soils with full degradation in topsoils in 2-5 days. Pterosin B dissipation followed the sum of two-first order reactions. The initial fast reaction with half-lives of 0.7-3.5 h contributed 11-59% of the total pterosin B degradation, while the slow reaction was 20-100 times slower than the fast reaction. Total dissipation half-lives were shorter for loamy sand (4 h) than for sandy loam soils (28 h). No degradation of pterosin B took place under sterile conditions assuming observed dissipation during the first 3 h could be attributed to irreversible sorption. Our results demonstrate that pterosin B is microbially degraded and that pterosin B is as unstable as ptaquiloside and hence cannot be used as an indicator for former presence of ptaquiloside in soil.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Skourti-Stathaki, Eirini","Clauson-Kaas, Frederik","Brandt, Kristian Koefoed","Rasmussen, Lars Holm","Hansen, Hans Chr. Bruun"],"cuid":["S02-098.27-039032"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Degradation kinetics","Microbial degradation","Natural toxins","Soil","Sorption"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dissipation of pterosin b in acid soils tracking the fate of the bracken fern carcinogen ptaquiloside","src":["kp","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.kp.dk/ws/files/37360012/Article_PTB_290816_LHRA_00000002_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-098.27-039032","identifier":[{"id":"27677121","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84988489895","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["kp-768007c0-e983-4f25-932d-625606683b95","ku-93ba730a-c6c5-4284-b294-6c51c32fcde8"],"keyword":["Degradation kinetics","Microbial degradation","Natural toxins","Soil","Sorption"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B4182410CF2FE0A7D3FD06BD51334CAA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.kp.dk/ws/files/37360012/Article_PTB_290816_LHRA_00000002_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen Metropol (ophørt), Laborantudd. og Professionsbach. i Laboratorietek. (ophørt)"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Eirini","key":"skourtistathakipau","last":"Skourti-Stathaki","name":"Skourti-Stathaki, Eirini","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Frederik","key":"clausonkaaspau","last":"Clauson-Kaas","locid":"309e1e9c-0ac3-432f-b88d-8531210e9b48","name":"Clauson-Kaas, Frederik","orcid":"0000-0002-4859-0148","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristian Koefoed","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"c196f0ea-2378-4bc3-bf49-2e64410cbabf","name":"Brandt, Kristian Koefoed","orcid":"0000-0001-7886-9708","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Holm","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"e7c0c08a-fea1-49c4-b828-c586042a355a","name":"Rasmussen, Lars Holm","orcid":"0000-0002-7301-3182","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans Chr. Bruun","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"9b553aa7-aebe-452e-b36f-b21edcff4e70","name":"Hansen, Hans Chr. Bruun","orcid":"0000-0002-8617-2393","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27677121"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.chemosphere.2016.09.050","issn":["00456535","18791298"],"issn_org":["00456535"],"journal":"Chemosphere","pages":"453-459","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Chemosphere","volume":"165"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84988489895"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","Universities","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-768007c0-e983-4f25-932d-625606683b95","ku-93ba730a-c6c5-4284-b294-6c51c32fcde8"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Dissipation of pterosin B in acid soils – Tracking the fate of the bracken fern carcinogen ptaquiloside","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.27-039032","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"author_count":6,"contributors":["Pedersen, Louise Holm","Nielsen, John E","Daugaard, Gedske","Hansen, Thomas v O","Rajpert-De Meyts, Ewa","Almstrup, Kristian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-421141"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"differences in global dna methylation of testicular seminoma are not associated with changes in histone modifications clinical prognosis i braf i mutations or gene expression","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-421141","identifier":[{"id":"85002251298","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27886677","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-2e7f02fa-10c2-4643-9bd8-5766c8f294fb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F61E111AC2D709280154ACB24375409A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Louise Holm","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Louise Holm","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"John E","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, John E","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Gedske","key":"daugaardpau","last":"Daugaard","locid":"db89ff2f-d030-4f0f-a11b-3981abe83992","name":"Daugaard, Gedske","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas v O","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Thomas v O","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ewa","key":"rajpertdemeytspau","last":"Rajpert-De Meyts","name":"Rajpert-De Meyts, Ewa","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristian","key":"almstruppau","last":"Almstrup","name":"Almstrup, Kristian","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27886677"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cancergen.2016.10.003","issn":["01654608","18734456"],"issn_org":["01654608"],"issue":"11","journal":"Cancer genetics and cytogenetics","pages":"506-514","status":"p","title":"Cancer genetics and cytogenetics","title_org":"Cancer genetics","volume":"209"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85002251298"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2e7f02fa-10c2-4643-9bd8-5766c8f294fb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Differences in global DNA methylation of testicular seminoma are not associated with changes in histone modifications, clinical prognosis, <i>BRAF</i> mutations or gene expression","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-421141","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"MicroRNAs (miRNAs) play a critical role in many biological processes and are aberrantly expressed in human cancers. Particular miRNAs function either as tumor suppressors or oncogenes and appear to have diagnostic and prognostic significance. Although numerous miRNAs are dys-regulated in colorectal cancer (CRC) only a small fraction has been characterized functionally. Using high-throughput functional screening and miRNA profiling of clinical samples the present study aims at identifying miRNAs important for the control of cellular growth and/or apoptosis in CRC. The high-throughput functional screening was carried out in six CRC cell lines transfected with a pre-miR library including 319 synthetic human pre-miRs. Phenotypic alterations were evaluated by immunostaining of cleaved cPARP (apoptosis) or MKI67 (proliferation). Additionally, TaqMan Human MicroRNA Array Set v2.0 was used to profile the expression of 667 miRNAs in 14 normal colon mucosa and 46 microsatellite stable stage II CRC patients. Among the miRNAs that induced growth arrest and apoptosis in the CRC cell lines, and at same time were dys-regulated in the clinical samples, miR-375 was selected for further analysis. Independent in vitro analysis of transient and stable transfected CRC cell lines confirmed that miR-375 reduces cell viability through the induction of apoptotic death. We identified YAP1 as a direct miR-375 target in CRC and show that HELLS and NOLC1 are down-stream targets. Knock-down of YAP1 mimicked the phenotype induced by miR-375 over-expression indicating that miR-375 most likely exerts its pro-apoptotic role through YAP1 and its anti-apoptotic down-stream targets BIRC5 and BCL2L1. Finally, in vivo analysis of mouse xenograft tumors showed that miR-375 expression significantly reduced tumor growth. We conclude that the high-throughput screening successfully identified miRNAs that induce apoptosis and/or inhibit proliferation in CRC cells. Finally, combining the functional screening with profiling of CRC tissue samples we identified clinically relevant miRNAs and miRNA targets in CRC.","author_count":25,"contributors":["Christensen, Lise Lotte","Holm, Anja","Rantala, Juha","Kallioniemi, Olli","Rasmussen, Mads Heilskov","Ostenfeld, Marie Stampe","Dagnæs-Hansen, Frederik","Øster, Bodil","Schepeler, Troels","Tobiasen, Heidi","Thorsen, Kasper","Sieber, Oliver M","Gibbs, Peter","Lamy, Philippe","Hansen, Torben F","Jakobsen, Anders","Riising, Eva M","Helin, Kristian","Lubinski, Jan","Hagemann-Madsen, Rikke","Laurberg, Søren","Ørntoft, Torben Falck","Andersen, Claus Lindbjerg"],"cuid":["S03-093.00-024446"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Finland","Poland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Pomeranian Medical University in Szczecin","University of Melbourne","VTT Technical Research Centre of Finland Ltd."],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Medical Biotechnology, VTT Technical Research Centre of Finland, Turku, Finland."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"functional screening identifies mirnas influencing apoptosis and proliferation in colorectal cancer","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0096767","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-093.00-024446","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4043686","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"24892549","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84902477980","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-a0e965b2-e8cb-4065-b037-0f9e964a7154","ku-60e846f7-721d-4d8c-afc7-01bc624